{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הנה בשמים עד\"י", :translit "hinneh ba-shamayim adi", :gloss "behold, in heaven עדי"} {:he "חנוך", :translit "chanokh", :gloss "Enoch"} {:he "שהד\"י", :translit "shehadi", :gloss "that עדי / the witness of"} {:he "מטטרון", :translit "metatron", :gloss "Metatron"} {:he "אחד מאותן של קודם דור המבול", :translit "echad me-otan shel kodem dor ha-mabul", :gloss "one of those from before the generation of the flood"} {:he "ואחד של אחר דור המבול", :translit "ve-echad shel acharei dor ha-mabul", :gloss "and one from after the generation of the flood"} {:he "חנוך ופנחס", :translit "chanokh u-pinchas", :gloss "Enoch and Phinehas"} {:he "והעלם לשמים", :translit "ve-he'elam la-shamayim", :gloss "and concealed them to heaven"} {:he "שיעידו עליו", :translit "she-ya'idu alav", :gloss "that they may testify concerning Him"} {:he "ובחר בחנוך", :translit "u-vachar be-chanokh", :gloss "and He chose Enoch"} {:he "שהיה דור שביעי", :translit "she-hayah dor shevi'i", :gloss "who was of the seventh generation"} {:he "שהקב\"ה חפץ בשביעיות", :translit "she-ha-kadosh baruch hu chafeitz be-shvi'iyot", :gloss "for the Holy One blessed be He desires seventhness"} {:he "וכן משה", :translit "u-chen mosheh", :gloss "so too Moses"} {:he "שהיה שביעי לאבות", :translit "she-hayah shevi'i la-avot", :gloss "who was seventh to the patriarchs"} {:he "ומשה עלה אל האלהים", :translit "u-mosheh alah el ha-elohim", :gloss "and Moses went up unto Elohim"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עד\"י", :b "חנוך"} {:kind :gematria, :a "שהד\"י", :b "מטטרון"}], :frame {:text "Enoch is described as walking with God and being taken by God (Genesis 5:24). The midrashic tradition identifies Enoch with Metatron, the angelic figure taken to heaven before the flood (Targum Yerushalmi to Genesis 5:24; b. Yevamot 16b debates whether Enoch is among the righteous taken). Phinehas is identified by rabbinic tradition with Elijah, who ascended to heaven after the flood-era (Sifrei Numbers 131; Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 47). Enoch is counted as the seventh from Adam (Genesis 5:1–24). The verse 'and Moses went up unto Elohim' appears at Exodus 19:3. Moses is counted as the seventh from Abraham: Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, Levi, Kohath, Amram, Moses (1 Chronicles 5:29–34 in the Hebrew, 6:1–3 in English).", :sources ["Genesis 5:24" "Genesis 5:1–24" "Exodus 19:3" "1 Chronicles 5:29–34" "Targum Yerushalmi to Genesis 5:24" "b. Yevamot 16b" "Sifrei Numbers 131" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 47"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "עד\"י", :a-value 84, :b "חנוך", :b-value 84, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "שהד\"י", :a-value 319, :b "מטטרון", :b-value 314, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:35.427511410Z", :model "glm-5.2"}